00:42:21.290 --> 00:42:22.250
How did you find Rob?

1013
00:42:22.810 --> 00:42:24.750
Well, I mean, you know Rob, right?

1014
00:42:24.790 --> 00:42:25.450
I know Rob.

1015
00:42:25.450 --> 00:42:29.730
We talked a little bit about it in one of our Fast Facts, but Rob wanted me to give

1016
00:42:29.730 --> 00:42:30.590
you a message.

1017
00:42:30.710 --> 00:42:30.890
Yeah.

1018
00:42:30.970 --> 00:42:33.910
Because I talked to him yesterday and he said, thank you so much.

1019
00:42:34.310 --> 00:42:36.990
Also, he's sorry that he couldn't say Lake Wall and Pawpuck.

1020
00:42:39.170 --> 00:42:41.870
Rob was, you know, in the Allison Jones orbit.

1021
00:42:42.250 --> 00:42:42.390
Yeah.

1022
00:42:42.410 --> 00:42:45.150
So, and we certainly knew about him.

1023
00:42:45.950 --> 00:42:49.670
And I don't know whether he came in for one of the other parts.

1024
00:42:49.810 --> 00:42:51.590
Like he might have come in for Dwight or something.

1025
00:42:51.730 --> 00:42:52.750
I'm not 100% sure.

1026
00:42:53.050 --> 00:42:54.010
Did that happen sometimes?

1027
00:42:54.010 --> 00:42:57.270
And sometimes people who had come in for main cast members, you would ping them for

1028
00:42:57.270 --> 00:42:58.230
a future episode.

1029
00:42:58.470 --> 00:42:58.710
Sure.

1030
00:42:58.970 --> 00:42:59.150
Yeah.

1031
00:42:59.150 --> 00:43:05.990
I mean, I think Allison released some of the audition tapes as part of a DVD extra, but

1032
00:43:05.990 --> 00:43:08.070
there were a lot of cool people that came in.

1033
00:43:08.130 --> 00:43:10.630
It would have been very interesting to see Seth Rogen as Dwight, for instance.

1034
00:43:10.910 --> 00:43:11.190
Yes.

1035
00:43:11.370 --> 00:43:11.690
Definitely.

1036
00:43:12.350 --> 00:43:13.870
Or Kristen Wiig as Pam.

1037
00:43:14.050 --> 00:43:14.170
Yeah.

1038
00:43:14.170 --> 00:43:15.590
I think she came in to read Pam.

1039
00:43:15.870 --> 00:43:16.010
Yeah.

1040
00:43:16.010 --> 00:43:19.070
I think she's in my sign, on my, on my, on my, Allison Jones.

1041
00:43:19.110 --> 00:43:19.490
And Catherine Hahn.

1042
00:43:19.670 --> 00:43:19.870
Yeah.

1043
00:43:20.310 --> 00:43:26.310
Allison Jones gave me my sign in sheet day and Catherine Hahn is on it and Bob Odenkirk

1044
00:43:26.310 --> 00:43:26.810
is on it.

1045
00:43:26.890 --> 00:43:27.030
Yeah.

1046
00:43:27.250 --> 00:43:29.750
Well, Bob was really the number two.

1047
00:43:29.890 --> 00:43:32.190
If we, if we didn't have Steve, it would have been Bob.

1048
00:43:32.350 --> 00:43:33.050
He did a great job.

1049
00:43:33.210 --> 00:43:36.190
And then in season nine, we brought him back as the sort of echo.

1050
00:43:36.410 --> 00:43:38.250
He was so fantastic too.

1051
00:43:38.430 --> 00:43:38.570
Yeah.

1052
00:43:39.470 --> 00:43:40.090
He's great.

1053
00:43:40.090 --> 00:43:43.130
So I have a lot of fan questions about the boat.

1054
00:43:43.330 --> 00:43:43.590
Sure.

1055
00:43:43.770 --> 00:43:44.010
Okay.

1056
00:43:44.430 --> 00:43:49.690
So since we're getting on the boat, Casey Wright asked, was the boat really moving?

1057
00:43:49.950 --> 00:43:52.570
And Sam Pellett asked how cold it was.

1058
00:43:52.750 --> 00:43:56.050
The boat was really moving through the water for one of the days of shooting.

1059
00:43:56.170 --> 00:43:59.470
The other two days, I believe it was docked and it was cold.

1060
00:43:59.470 --> 00:44:04.590
It was December, 2005, which was chilly, especially at night out on the water.

1061
00:44:04.810 --> 00:44:08.370
A lot of people wondered, were you pretending to be that cold?

1062
00:44:08.370 --> 00:44:10.410
I remember being cold.

1063
00:44:10.710 --> 00:44:10.770
I don't think, yeah, yes.

1064
00:44:11.150 --> 00:44:12.670
I don't think there was a lot of pretending.

1065
00:44:12.670 --> 00:44:15.330
Your cheeks are like bright pink in that scene.

1066
00:44:15.510 --> 00:44:15.870
Yes.

1067
00:44:16.210 --> 00:44:22.870
So Lorne Michaels has a thing that he says sometimes where like he will get in character

1068
00:44:22.870 --> 00:44:24.650
underwear for the actors.

1069
00:44:25.170 --> 00:44:25.430
Oh.

1070
00:44:26.270 --> 00:44:27.890
And yeah, I think this is it.

1071
00:44:28.590 --> 00:44:29.990
And people will say, well, why?

1072
00:44:30.110 --> 00:44:30.570
Who cares?

1073
00:44:30.690 --> 00:44:31.770
It's not going to be on camera.

1074
00:44:31.850 --> 00:44:33.030
And he goes, yes, but the actors know.

1075
00:44:34.030 --> 00:44:35.290
I kind of get that.

1076
00:44:35.350 --> 00:44:35.510
Yeah.

1077
00:44:35.830 --> 00:44:36.910
I kind of get that.

1078
00:44:36.910 --> 00:44:41.790
And so we certainly believed in that and went out on this real boat in Long Beach Harbor

1079
00:44:41.790 --> 00:44:42.890
and it was this huge thing.

1080
00:44:43.170 --> 00:44:52.830
And to me, the key of it was that romantic scene on the top deck between Pam and Jim.

1081
00:44:54.950 --> 00:44:59.590
And I just thought it'd be so pretty up there with the twinkling lights of the harbor in

1082
00:44:59.590 --> 00:45:00.430
the background and everything.

1083
00:45:00.430 --> 00:45:08.190
So we do that scene and later in the editing room, somebody was like, what'd you do?

1084
00:45:08.310 --> 00:45:13.350
Did you just put a row of Christmas lights against a black piece of duveteen there and

1085
00:45:13.350 --> 00:45:14.310
do it in a studio?

1086
00:45:14.450 --> 00:45:14.970
And we're like, no.

1087
00:45:16.230 --> 00:45:17.590
We're on a boat.

1088
00:45:17.690 --> 00:45:18.790
We're on an actual boat.

1089
00:45:18.850 --> 00:45:20.970
But it didn't really look that impressive.

1090
00:45:21.170 --> 00:45:26.030
When it came down, it was just this one little twinkle thing of lights on the horizon.

1091
00:45:26.270 --> 00:45:27.390
Like we could have been on a soundstage.

1092
00:45:27.390 --> 00:45:29.410
Yeah, we could have been nice and toasty and comfortable.

1093
00:45:29.570 --> 00:45:31.850
But the wind was blowing and I could, I don't know.

1094
00:45:31.930 --> 00:45:32.950
I could tell you're on a boat.

1095
00:45:33.110 --> 00:45:33.830
I think so.

1096
00:45:34.190 --> 00:45:37.150
Well, one of the challenges of being on the boat was how sick everyone got.

1097
00:45:37.330 --> 00:45:38.310
Greg, do you remember that?

1098
00:45:38.670 --> 00:45:39.210
We were all really sick.

1099
00:45:39.210 --> 00:45:40.510
Yeah, there was a lot of seasickness.

1100
00:45:40.710 --> 00:45:40.810
Yeah.

1101
00:45:40.890 --> 00:45:42.450
Rain puked a lot.

1102
00:45:42.770 --> 00:45:42.910
Yeah.

1103
00:45:43.950 --> 00:45:45.750
I did not get seasick.

1104
00:45:45.950 --> 00:45:50.650
But do you remember coming up to Kate Flannery and I and saying, hey, you guys, I want to

1105
00:45:50.650 --> 00:45:53.870
get some B-roll of people vomiting off the side of the boat.

1106
00:45:54.070 --> 00:45:54.790
Greg, do you remember?

1107
00:45:54.790 --> 00:45:56.290
I don't, but that would be something I would have done.

1108
00:45:56.350 --> 00:45:57.730
It was like three in the morning.

1109
00:45:57.890 --> 00:46:01.770
And you said, so you had Matt Stone grab as many people as he could.

1110
00:46:01.890 --> 00:46:04.930
And we had the choice of cream of mushroom or minestrone.

1111
00:46:05.370 --> 00:46:06.350
Oh, right, right, right.

1112
00:46:06.550 --> 00:46:07.270
The fake vomiting.

1113
00:46:07.270 --> 00:46:08.030
The fake vomiting.

1114
00:46:08.190 --> 00:46:08.850
The fake vomiting.

1115
00:46:08.850 --> 00:46:11.530
And I did minestrone.

1116
00:46:11.790 --> 00:46:12.510
Yeah, good choice.

1117
00:46:12.790 --> 00:46:18.190
But you had to take a swig of it and hold it in your mouth until action and then puke

1118
00:46:18.190 --> 00:46:18.330
it.

1119
00:46:18.690 --> 00:46:24.530
And the, I don't know, five to 10 seconds you held it in your mouth was the most horrible

1120
00:46:24.530 --> 00:46:28.050
thing because you were just like, like trying not to gag.

1121
00:46:28.470 --> 00:46:32.350
So I didn't puke for real, but I did fake puke.

1122
00:46:32.470 --> 00:46:33.930
Well, I got really sick.

1123
00:46:34.090 --> 00:46:34.930
So did David Denman.

1124
00:46:36.050 --> 00:46:38.150
And I was wearing those wristbands.

1125
00:46:38.150 --> 00:46:41.190
We were trying to pass out boning too or stuff.

1126
00:46:41.410 --> 00:46:44.490
Yeah, there was all, there were all these remedies, but nothing really works.

1127
00:46:44.710 --> 00:46:45.330
Seasickness, gum.

1128
00:46:45.330 --> 00:46:46.790
Someone gave me something to chew on.

1129
00:46:47.170 --> 00:46:48.190
Maybe the gum.

1130
00:46:48.410 --> 00:46:48.550
Yeah.

1131
00:46:48.690 --> 00:46:49.850
There's like a ginger gum.

1132
00:46:50.670 --> 00:46:56.330
So at one point, the real captain of the boat heard that I was struggling.

1133
00:46:56.690 --> 00:46:56.830
So there were three captains.

1134
00:46:56.910 --> 00:46:57.630
There were three captains.

1135
00:46:58.470 --> 00:47:04.710
And then there was also, there was Dwight steering the ship and a guy and then a real guy.

1136
00:47:05.070 --> 00:47:10.290
At one point, the real captain of the ship heard I was struggling and he got out this

1137
00:47:10.290 --> 00:47:13.690
oil that he rubbed behind my ears.

1138
00:47:14.350 --> 00:47:17.330
And about 10 minutes later, I was totally fine.

1139
00:47:17.330 --> 00:47:18.010
Wow.

1140
00:47:18.190 --> 00:47:19.790
So I had written about this in my diary.

1141
00:47:19.790 --> 00:47:21.990
I looked it up and I found some on Amazon.

1142
00:47:22.250 --> 00:47:23.310
Here's what's in it.

1143
00:47:23.650 --> 00:47:28.530
Here's where we turn this whole thing into an essential oils pitch podcaSt.

1144
00:47:28.930 --> 00:47:29.590
By the way.

1145
00:47:29.730 --> 00:47:31.090
We're sponsored by.

1146
00:47:31.250 --> 00:47:31.430
Yeah.

1147
00:47:31.850 --> 00:47:32.850
Sold by Jan.

1148
00:47:33.310 --> 00:47:34.870
Jan's essential oils and candles.

1149
00:47:35.110 --> 00:47:36.170
So here's what it has in it.

1150
00:47:36.590 --> 00:47:43.890
Lavender, peppermint, chamomile, something called ylang-ylang, birch.

1151
00:47:43.890 --> 00:47:46.930
And then it has frankincense and myrrh.

1152
00:47:47.270 --> 00:47:49.630
That's the stuff that the wise men gave to Jesus.

1153
00:47:49.990 --> 00:47:50.040
Yeah.

1154
00:47:50.040 --> 00:47:50.370
I know.

1155
00:47:50.530 --> 00:47:51.250
Two of the things.

1156
00:47:51.550 --> 00:47:52.470
Very expensive stuff.

1157
00:47:52.550 --> 00:47:52.890
Yeah.

1158
00:47:53.750 --> 00:47:54.190
Fancy.

1159
00:47:54.230 --> 00:47:54.990
Who knew?

1160
00:47:55.310 --> 00:47:59.910
I didn't even, I mean, I know frankincense and myrrh are real, but-

1161
00:47:59.910 --> 00:48:00.910
I didn't know they were real.

1162
00:48:01.130 --> 00:48:02.030
I mean-

1163
00:48:02.030 --> 00:48:03.950
I thought they were part of a Christmas song.

1164
00:48:04.370 --> 00:48:05.390
That's not real.

1165
00:48:05.590 --> 00:48:07.710
But like, what are they?

1166
00:48:07.910 --> 00:48:10.390
I guess they are what you rub behind your ears when you're seasick.

1167
00:48:10.810 --> 00:48:13.770
It sounds like they just threw everything in the kitchen sink into this.

1168
00:48:13.890 --> 00:48:14.330
They did.

1169
00:48:14.790 --> 00:48:16.050
The ylang-ylang?

1170
00:48:16.190 --> 00:48:16.850
I don't know.

1171
00:48:17.090 --> 00:48:17.330
Ylang-ylang.

1172
00:48:17.410 --> 00:48:18.290
Ylang-ylang.

1173
00:48:18.550 --> 00:48:18.970
All right.

1174
00:48:19.070 --> 00:48:25.570
So in the script, there was a scene, Greg, that as the boat is pulling away, Toby's car

1175
00:48:25.570 --> 00:48:33.870
suddenly drives up and he, and Michael yells at him from the ship, oh, come on, what's

1176
00:48:33.870 --> 00:48:33.970
up?

1177
00:48:34.030 --> 00:48:37.490
And he's like, I'm sorry, there was an accident or there was traffic.

1178
00:48:37.490 --> 00:48:39.930
And then Michael says, we're not going back.

1179
00:48:40.110 --> 00:48:40.850
We're not going back for him.

1180
00:48:40.910 --> 00:48:41.530
Just leave him.

1181
00:48:41.650 --> 00:48:46.150
And then Paul turns to camera as Toby and he kind of gives a little wink.

1182
00:48:46.250 --> 00:48:46.850
Yeah, it's a big smile.

1183
00:48:46.870 --> 00:48:47.690
Yeah, like he did it on purpose.

1184
00:48:47.850 --> 00:48:49.490
But you can find that in the deleted scenes.

1185
00:48:49.490 --> 00:48:50.150
We shot it.

1186
00:48:50.230 --> 00:48:50.470
Yes.

1187
00:48:50.590 --> 00:48:51.130
We shot it.

1188
00:48:51.190 --> 00:48:51.750
And it was very nice.

1189
00:48:51.850 --> 00:48:54.890
And that is why Toby is not on the boat for anyone who was wondering.

1190
00:48:55.270 --> 00:48:56.130
Maybe we should take-

1191
00:48:56.130 --> 00:49:01.530
There's a lot of excuses for why Toby wouldn't be on things so that he could help out as

1192
00:49:01.530 --> 00:49:02.690
a writer and producer.

1193
00:49:03.170 --> 00:49:05.110
Toby and BJ and Mindy.

1194
00:49:05.330 --> 00:49:05.430
Yeah.

1195
00:49:05.430 --> 00:49:08.610
Like they sat in the, you know, Mindy was in the annex, like things like that.

1196
00:49:08.610 --> 00:49:13.990
I thought I was so clever in season one making them actors so that they would have this experience

1197
00:49:13.990 --> 00:49:14.850
of being actors.

1198
00:49:14.870 --> 00:49:19.810
And then at some point in season two, I'm looking around and 50% of the writers are gone

1199
00:49:19.810 --> 00:49:20.990
because they're on set.

1200
00:49:21.110 --> 00:49:22.130
And I'm like, oh, what have I done?

1201
00:49:24.710 --> 00:49:25.110
Okay.

1202
00:49:25.250 --> 00:49:28.630
At seven minutes, 55 seconds, Rob Riggle breaks.

1203
00:49:28.810 --> 00:49:29.950
He totally breaks.

1204
00:49:30.150 --> 00:49:30.310
What?

1205
00:49:30.410 --> 00:49:31.170
We talked about it.

1206
00:49:31.170 --> 00:49:32.970
It just, it stayed in the shot.

1207
00:49:33.250 --> 00:49:37.610
So Rob as Captain Jack is going over the safety features of the boat.

1208
00:49:38.190 --> 00:49:41.610
And Michael really wants to hijack this speech and give it.

1209
00:49:41.770 --> 00:49:43.110
And he can't.

1210
00:49:43.190 --> 00:49:46.670
So he just starts doing like the flight attendant, like pointing to the exits.

1211
00:49:46.870 --> 00:49:47.010
Yeah.

1212
00:49:47.210 --> 00:49:48.230
And Rob just breaks.

1213
00:49:48.490 --> 00:49:50.430
He just starts laughing, but he just keeps going.

1214
00:49:50.670 --> 00:49:52.590
And then Rain as Dwight laughs.

1215
00:49:52.770 --> 00:49:54.830
And so it just sort of like, but it stays in.

1216
00:49:54.990 --> 00:49:55.910
Oh, that's amazing.

1217
00:49:56.190 --> 00:49:58.270
But Rob was like, yeah, I just laughed.

1218
00:49:58.430 --> 00:50:00.530
But I just kept talking through my laugh.

1219
00:50:00.530 --> 00:50:02.870
When Steve is doing his dancing.

1220
00:50:03.190 --> 00:50:03.570
Yes.

1221
00:50:03.750 --> 00:50:09.750
That I remember like trying to build the reactions because everybody's supposed to be like unimpressed

1222
00:50:09.750 --> 00:50:12.430
and just, you know, straight faced.

1223
00:50:12.430 --> 00:50:16.690
And it was almost impossible because everybody was breaking.

1224
00:50:17.030 --> 00:50:19.050
He made him do that over and over and over again.

1225
00:50:19.170 --> 00:50:20.450
For so long.

1226
00:50:20.550 --> 00:50:20.670
Yeah.

1227
00:50:20.670 --> 00:50:24.610
That's, I remember, I was, I remember when we rewatched it, I just wrote, oh my gosh,

1228
00:50:24.730 --> 00:50:27.050
Michael's dance because he danced for so long.

1229
00:50:27.250 --> 00:50:27.300
Yeah.

1230
00:50:27.300 --> 00:50:30.790
In my journal, I said that we started taping that around 2 a.m.

1231
00:50:30.790 --> 00:50:32.510
Like it was really late.

1232
00:50:33.110 --> 00:50:33.270
Yeah.

1233
00:50:33.510 --> 00:50:36.410
A fan question from Tara Leitchkey.

1234
00:50:37.410 --> 00:50:39.770
Was Steve's dance choreographed?

1235
00:50:40.550 --> 00:50:41.710
I don't think so.

1236
00:50:41.870 --> 00:50:43.630
I really think he improvised that.

1237
00:50:43.870 --> 00:50:45.630
I don't remember it being in the script.

1238
00:50:45.830 --> 00:50:48.410
I think he just kind of went for it.

1239
00:50:48.590 --> 00:50:53.730
I have the script at home for this episode and I read it and there is no direction for

1240
00:50:53.730 --> 00:50:54.670
Michael's dance in the script.

1241
00:50:54.670 --> 00:50:58.210
It just says, pan over to see Michael doing a weird dance.

1242
00:50:58.450 --> 00:50:58.710
Yeah.

1243
00:50:58.830 --> 00:50:59.230
That's it.

1244
00:50:59.390 --> 00:51:01.830
That's as much as there was.

1245
00:51:02.390 --> 00:51:04.110
Another fan question about the dance.

1246
00:51:04.310 --> 00:51:11.710
Steve Dresser says, how many takes of that superb dance did it take to get Steve's full moves?

1247
00:51:11.910 --> 00:51:13.790
I'm going to say about six, I think.

1248
00:51:13.910 --> 00:51:14.090
Yeah.

1249
00:51:14.270 --> 00:51:14.910
What do you think?

1250
00:51:15.010 --> 00:51:15.610
What do you remember?

1251
00:51:15.890 --> 00:51:17.010
That seems about right.

1252
00:51:17.250 --> 00:51:20.390
I can't remember when he started slapping his legs.

1253
00:51:20.390 --> 00:51:21.390
Yeah, that was amazing.

1254
00:51:21.510 --> 00:51:23.250
If that was early on or later.

1255
00:51:23.250 --> 00:51:24.310
And the worm.

1256
00:51:24.490 --> 00:51:25.350
I mean, they were different.

1257
00:51:25.490 --> 00:51:29.610
I feel like there were different versions of the dance and then we kind of made the highlight

1258
00:51:29.610 --> 00:51:29.930
reel.

1259
00:51:30.210 --> 00:51:30.350
Yes.

1260
00:51:30.750 --> 00:51:30.950
Yeah.

1261
00:51:31.210 --> 00:51:36.230
And on the deleted scenes, you can see even more of the dancing if you want to.

1262
00:51:36.410 --> 00:51:39.510
I remember when Ken finally was like, okay, cut.

1263
00:51:39.830 --> 00:51:42.230
Steve was on the ground doing the last worm.

1264
00:51:42.230 --> 00:51:43.030
Yeah, that was the last one.

1265
